  "response": "## The finding\n\n`crimes_00032` — **SVG With Embedded Raster**, severity `high`, confidence `0.95`, on `src/assets/partner-logo.svg`. Verbatim from the evidence:\n\n- **\"2 `<image href=\"data:image/…;base64,…\">` occurrences\"**\n- **\"embedded MIME types: image/jpeg, image/png\"**\n- **\"SVG byte size: 592 bytes (includes the base64 overhead)\"**\n- **\"re-author the raster region as vector paths, or split it out to its own asset\"**\n\nSo: two rasters, one **image/png** and one **image/jpeg**, inside a 200×80 file that advertises itself as vector.\n\n## What's actually in the file\n\n```\nviewBox=\"0 0 200 80\"\n  <image x=\"0\"   y=\"0\" width=\"80\" height=\"80\" href=\"data:image/png;base64,…\"/>       ← left slot\n  <image x=\"100\" y=\"0\" width=\"80\" height=\"80\" xlink:href=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,…\"/> ← right slot\n```\n\nTwo 80×80 slots with a 20px gutter, and a `<title>Partner logo</title>`. There is no vector geometry at all — the file is a base64 envelope with an `.svg` extension.\n\nTwo things the detector doesn't say that change the plan:\n\n1. **The MIME types tell you which slot is salvageable.** PNG at icon scale is alpha'd flat art — that's a logo mark, and logo marks always have a vector original. JPEG is lossy and opaque with no alpha channel; nobody exports a logo mark as JPEG. Slot B is almost certainly photographic (a partner headshot, product shot, or a screenshot-derived badge) and is *not* re-authorable as paths.\n2. **The second `<image>` uses `xlink:href` but the root declares no `xmlns:xlink`.** That's an undeclared namespace prefix — strict XML parsers reject the document, and the modern `href` on the first element vs. legacy `xlink:href` on the second means this file was assembled by two different tools. Fix it while you're in there.\n\n## Remediation\n\n**Step 1 — recover the vector source for slot A.** The PNG at `x=0` is the partner's mark. Get the original from Figma/Illustrator/the partner's brand kit and export as SVG with *\"flatten/outline text\"* on, so the wordmark ships as paths rather than a font dependency you don't control. Paste those `<path>` elements in at `x=0`, sized into the existing 80×80 box. This slot should end up as pure geometry — no `<image>`.\n\n**Step 2 — split slot B out to a standalone raster.** Decode the JPEG and look at it. If it's genuinely photographic, do not try to trace it — an auto-traced photo produces a multi-hundred-KB path soup that renders worse than the JPEG did. Extract it to `src/assets/partner-photo.webp` (WebP at q80, sized to the rendered 80×80 at 2× = 160×160, with a `.png` fallback only if you still support browsers that need it).\n\n**Step 3 — do *not* reference that raster back from inside the SVG.** This is the trap in the obvious fix. Replacing the data URI with `<image href=\"./partner-photo.webp\">` looks correct and breaks silently: when an SVG is loaded via `<img src>`, as a CSS `background-image`, or in an `<object>`, external resource loading is blocked by the SVG secure-static mode — the slot renders empty. It only works if the SVG is inlined into the DOM. Compose the two in markup instead:\n\n```html\n<span class=\"partner-logo\">\n  <img src=\"/assets/partner-logo.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"80\" height=\"80\">\n  <img src=\"/assets/partner-photo.webp\" alt=\"Partner name\" width=\"80\" height=\"80\" loading=\"lazy\">\n</span>\n```\n\nThe SVG keeps its own 80×80 viewBox once slot B leaves; the 20px gutter becomes a `gap` in CSS, which is where layout belonged anyway.\n\n**Step 4 — clean up the envelope.** Drop the now-unused `xlink` reference (or declare `xmlns:xlink` if anything still needs it), retighten `viewBox` to `0 0 80 80`, keep `<title>`, and add `role=\"img\"` so assistive tech announces it.\n\n### Files after the refactor\n\n| File | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| `src/assets/partner-logo.svg` | vector paths only, `viewBox=\"0 0 80 80\"`, zero `<image>` elements |\n| `src/assets/partner-photo.webp` | the ex-JPEG, resized to its rendered dimensions |\n| consuming component / CSS | composes the two side by side with the 20px gutter |\n\nThe logo still ships — it just ships as an actual vector plus one honestly-labelled raster.\n\n## One thing worth checking first\n\n`grep` across the fixture finds **zero references** to `partner-logo.svg` (or to `src/assets/` at all), which matches the finding's `blast_radius_importers: 0`. So before step 3, confirm how this asset reaches production — a build-time glob, a CMS, or a partner-facing download. If it's consumed as a bare `<img src>` by something outside this repo, step 3's markup composition needs to happen wherever that consumer lives, and slot B may need to stay a separate deliverable you hand over rather than an in-repo component.\n\nI can do steps 2 and 4 mechanically right now (decode, re-encode, clean the envelope). Step 1 needs the design source — I can't invent the partner's paths from a 1×1 placeholder pixel.",
